{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ולא תחטיא", :translit "v'lo tachati", :gloss "and you shall not cause to sin"} {:he "כי יקח איש אשה", :translit "ki yikach ish isha", :gloss "when a man takes a wife"} {:he "שהיא מצלת את האדם מן החטא", :translit "shehi matzilat et ha-adam min hachet", :gloss "that she saves the person from sin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: juxtaposition of adjacent verses as a hermeneutic link"}], :frame {:text "The principle that marriage protects a person from sin is rooted in the blessing recited at a wedding, which cites Proverbs 18:22: 'He who finds a wife has found good, and obtains favor from YHWH.' The Sages interpret this to mean that marriage draws a person away from transgression, as expressed in the statement that one who marries has fulfilled half of the injunction to be fruitful and multiply (Sotah 4b). The juxtaposition of 'you shall not cause to sin' with the verse 'when a man takes a wife' reinforces that a wife is the remedy for the evil inclination (Yevamot 63a).", :sources ["Proverbs 18:22" "Yevamot 63a" "Sotah 4b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "נחלה", :translit "nachalah", :gloss "heritage"} {:he "כי יקח", :translit "ki yikach", :gloss "when he takes"} {:he "בית והון נחלת אבות וגומר", :translit "bayit v'chon nachalat avot v'gomer", :gloss "house and wealth heritage of fathers and so on"} {:he "כי יקח איש אשה מה' אשה משכלת", :translit "ki yikach ish isha mei-hashem isha maskelet", :gloss "when a man takes a wife from YHWH a wife of understanding"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: juxtaposition of adjacent verses as a hermeneutic link"}], :frame {:text "The verse in Proverbs 19:14 states: 'House and wealth are the heritage of fathers, but a prudent wife is from YHWH,' contrasting earthly inheritance with divine gift. The halakhah that a woman's ketubah may be collected from landed property is rooted in the Mishnah's discussion of ketubah collection (Ketubot 78b–79a). Property can be acquired through three methods: kesef (money), shetar (document), and chazakah (possession), as codified in the opening of tractate Kiddushin (Kiddushin 26a). The Ba'al HaTurim leverages the verbal proximity of 'heritage' and 'when a man takes' to connect these laws.", :sources ["Proverbs 19:14" "Ketubot 78b" "Kiddushin 26a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: juxtaposition of adjacent verses as a hermeneutic link", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "semikhut: juxtaposition of adjacent verses as a hermeneutic link", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:57.111221904Z", :model "glm-5.2"}